PARMGREP(1)                    ZOAU Command Syntax                   PARMGREP(1)

NAME

	parmgrep - Search for a string across the parmlib concatenation.

SYNOPSIS

	parmgrep [-dhinv] <str> <dataset-pattern>

	-d
	 	Print out debug messages.

	 -h
	 	Display syntax help.

	 -i
	 	Ignore case.

	 -n
	 	Display line numbers.

	 -v
	 	Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	Search for a string across the parmlib concatenation matching a pattern.

DATASET PATTERNS

	The following rules apply to <dataset-pattern>.

	The high-level qualifier (HLQ) must be specified in full.
	An asterisk (*) matches any sequence of characters.
	A question mark (?) matches a single character.

EXAMPLES

	Search for 'rdtd' (case sensitive) across the parmlib concatenation.

		parmgrep rdtd

 	Search for Hello (case insensitive) across the parmlib concatenation,
	displaying line numbers.

		parmgrep -in Hello

EXIT VALUES

	0
		parmgrep completed successfully.

	Other
		Error, see message for details.

SEE ALSO

	parmwhence(1), procgrep(1)
